TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c12","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"closest any literature candidate comes to the filtration language -- construction filtered by x (primes p <= x), x -> infinity is a sieve-limit, and the Weil form restricted to support <= S is a finite face-sum object","checksum":"6b230951308ff56e6cbc9f62294f986997ec15f44593dc9bd08cb88296389bd6","id":"B1","limits":"the operator is built from primes alone (forward), but the eigenvalue<->zero identification is numerical, not derived; D2: 'striking numerical accuracy' needs quantified error bars (the reported 'first 50 zeros to 2.6e-55...1e-3' figures are secondary-source -- GitHub summary of Connes, J. Open Math. Probl. Apr 2026 -- treat as unverified until the primary is read); D12: audit the rank-one perturbation direction -- prime-derived (Weil-form eigenvectors, principled) vs zero-fitted is THE question for replication","type":"B","x":"B's construction: D_log^{(lam,N)} filtered by x (primes p <= x)","y":"the work's Delta_z filtration language"},{"buys":"the geometric side = sum over places p in S with prime terms = face-sum over the place set; limit S -> all places ~ z -> infinity","checksum":"79010444de0d4a16e93755ccb5680e4ef26a83d84b965ddf223bfbb4891b24b7","id":"B2","limits":"reformulation, not derivation -- the hard direction (Weil positivity = RH) is imported, not derived from counting; this is the D10-shaped move at the highest level of sophistication","type":"B","x":"A's semilocal cutoff (finite place set S): a place-filtration, adding places one at a time","y":"the work's z-filtration Delta_z"},{"buys":"existence proof that the Hilbert-Polya dream is coherent in the hyperbolic world -- the one world where the full dream works (trace formula derived, zeros = Laplacian eigenvalues, positivity geometric)","checksum":"d2dd8a90fde52d8dee976f7e4f0baa5f3aed86936684bf204c1b37a05e3c4123","id":"B3","limits":"already closed as the D10d function-field template; it needs actual hyperbolic dynamics, which the Riemann-zeta case lacks (that absence is what kills E)","type":"B","x":"Mayer transfer operator L_s with det(1+-L_s) identities for Selberg zeta","y":"the full Hilbert-Polya dream"},{"checksum":"eaf37ad7726d7b6ce77bf66701390432ac066605496120e5798a44d0d83b3323","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"Deninger program: Theta, infinitesimal generator of a flow on conjectural leafwise cohomology H^1, with zeta(s) = det_reg(s - Theta|H^1); the explicit formula would become a Lefschetz trace formula (primes = closed orbits of length log p, matching the Guinand-Weil prime-power terms)","note":"The space is missing -- rational Witt space constructions exist as fragments. Positivity would come from Hodge/index positivity on the conjectural cohomology (analogue of Weil's intersection pairing) -- does not exist yet. The orbit list is put in, not derived from a sieve process; finite-orbit truncation (length <= log z) is a sieve-like cutoff. The 2024 theorem (arXiv:2410.20758) proves Deninger's conjectured regularized-determinant formula in the dynamical setting -- the template, not Spec Z.","status":"conjectural","type":"C"},{"checksum":"a1ba2b58d8a63c36abce0590990b700d63045d64788716685093565e9e034728","id":"C2","kind":"claim","label":"Self-adjointness buys 'spectrum is real,' not 'spectrum is the zeros' -- B's eigenvalue<->zero identification remains conjectural","note":"B is the only candidate attempting the literal Hilbert-Polya statement with self-adjointness proved (via Caratheodory-Fejer/Toeplitz extension theory); its positivity source (self-adjointness of D_log) is genuine by construction and forces a real spectrum. Input is prime Euler products only -- counting-born, forward. But 'limit = the zeros' is numerical ('convergence as N, lam -> infinity unproved -- a strategy toward a proof'). MIXED: counting-born input, conjectural identification.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"2b1f6cdf1ef537fc2545daa7683538191b5ae9bdeaa01f477df888879dab7023","id":"G1","result":"zeros ABSENT -- spectrum is {log n}; no eigenvalues, no resonances. The pole of zeta at beta=1 appears as the KMS phase transition (unique KMS state for beta<=1, Galois-indexed extremal states for beta>1). Disqualified as a zero-operator at the gate. (Planat et al. restate RH as a KMS phase-operator inequality -- RH-equivalent by construction, a D10 move layered on top.)","title":"C. Bost-Connes system (1995) + Julia (1990) precursor -- KILLED as zero-operator","transfer":"survives as the canonical 'zeta from counting' machine (gets the pole right) -- sharpens the question of what machine gets the zeros. Sources: Bost-Connes 1995; Planat-Sole-Omar, hal-00549030","tried":"Hecke C*-algebra of Q-lattices up to scale; GNS space l^2(N); operator H|n> = (log n)|n>; partition function Z(beta) = Tr e^{-beta H} = zeta(beta)","type":"G","verdict":"fails at the gate -- no zeros in the machine"},{"checksum":"bd546aad8836d8a65bba310c5021f68dbcec49cf477fb637337d2f5910209463","id":"G2","result":"does not exist independently -- transfer operators (Mayer's L_s, det(1+-L_s) identities) work where a hyperbolic dynamical system exists, and for the Riemann zeta 'the dynamical system with prime periodic orbits' IS Deninger's missing space (candidate D). Type-error firewall: 'prime orbit' (primitive periodic orbit) != rational prime; proposals sliding between the two senses equivocate","title":"E. Ruelle transfer operator for the 'prime dynamical system' -- KILLED as independent candidate","transfer":"reduces to D. The Selberg/Mayer case stands as the control: the one world where the full dream works (trace formula derived, zeros = Laplacian eigenvalues, positivity geometric) = the already-closed D10d function-field template. Source: Mayer transfer operator / Selberg zeta (arXiv:1008.4229) as the working template","tried":"Mayer transfer operator template applied to a 'prime dynamical system'","type":"G","verdict":"no dynamics, no transfer operator -- reduces to D"},{"checksum":"03c81e46006df25506a1bbb03c4571c664f0f14d5eaedb8d96e8fdc80e01a0f8","id":"G3","result":"NOT eigenvalues. Models reproduce the SMOOTH counting function Nbar(E) only (Connes absorption as lowest-Landau-level limit); higher Landau levels 'suggested' for fluctuations -- heuristic. Same ceiling as 11a (Berry-Keating as formulated). The 2025 Rindler/Majorana zero-eigenvalue claims tune the quantization condition to zeta -- D10-flavored","title":"F. Sierra xp-regularizations -- KILLED as zero-operators","transfer":"the Landau-limit unification of Berry-Keating and Connes regularizations is elegant physics -- background only. Sources: Sierra-Townsend arXiv:0805.4079; Sierra arXiv:0712.0705; Rindler/Majorana xp-class variants (e.g. arXiv:2503.09644)","tried":"planar charged particle (E = V_0 xy + uniform B), lowest Landau level; or 1+1D Rindler/Majorana spinor spaces; Landau Hamiltonian / xp-class Hermitian H = sqrt(x) p-hat sqrt(x) + a^{-2} sqrt(x) p-hat^{-1} sqrt(x) with domain choices for self-adjointness","type":"G","verdict":"smooth-count ceiling -- genuine positivity (ordinary QM spectral positivity), irrelevant to RH"},{"checksum":"e7d5749478a38a22231ddffaa4653a908303a6a6e278a79d6f380a2202a9300e","id":"G4","result":"claimed eigenvalues via eigenfunctions psi_z(x) = -zeta(z, x+1) (Hurwitz zeta) -- the answer inserted by hand (D10 textbook case). PT-symmetry does not guarantee real eigenvalues; self-adjointness unproved (Bellissard criticism). The 'positivity' is the unproved claim itself","title":"G. Bender-Brody-Mueller PT-symmetric operator (2017) -- KILLED","transfer":"fails the self-adjointness requirement at face value. Sources: Bender-Brody-Mueller, PRL 2017; Bellissard criticism; Wikipedia Hilbert-Polya survey","tried":"H-hat = (1-e^{-i p-hat})^{-1} (x-hat p-hat + p-hat x-hat) (1-e^{-i p-hat}) on L^2(R), PT-symmetric (pseudo-Hermitian)","type":"G","verdict":"answer inserted by hand, reality of spectrum unproved, not self-adjoint"},{"checksum":"fee53c67a32c89ddf73d9ba901cc05c701b75cce22ae62b6e83af5e411ab49cc","id":"G5","result":"zeros = eigenvalues BY CONSTRUCTION -- zeros are the input. Purest D10 violation on the list; the inverse problem always succeeds and teaches nothing. Jaksch (2025, arXiv:2510.16759) explains the famous fractal D~1.5 as an artifact of the Riemann-von Mangoldt approximation error -- the 'fractal' was error signal, and the kill is now self-explaining","title":"H. Wu-Sprung inverse potential (1990s) -- KILLED","transfer":"canonical warning: any 'operator from zeros' fit must pass the forward-direction test (primes in, spectrum out). Sources: Wu-Sprung 1990s; Jaksch, arXiv:2510.16759","tried":"1D Schrodinger -d^2/dx^2 + V(x) on L^2(R), V reconstructed numerically from the first 500 zeros","type":"G","verdict":"inverse tautology -- with the kill now self-explaining (fractal = approximation error)"},{"checksum":"e3d1c1e6f07480d5526a1f8194c6e03e770d4a22c3f7e4e965f33e75f7872f3b","from":"B1","id":"L1","rel":"supports","to":"V2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"5946d5d9f6349c8c7c414217423b332826fcf927f070052cc648a70641a17e70","from":"B2","id":"L2","rel":"supports","to":"V1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"863c62a9197b29ea9d17d1585ee0be062beb91820b755cefe5d3e0e1b52ede98","from":"G2","id":"L3","rel":"depends_on","to":"C1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"e4fc02ed9eb540feb7ae6a1a113e98e65698f22150c12969b278136ef6976e5f","from":"B3","id":"L4","rel":"supports","to":"V4","type":"L"},{"checksum":"fc2b56b866c82beb7dec2b4a933acc946595b37ee18000499b7c486e4595f27c","from":"C1","id":"L5","rel":"supports","to":"V3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"f8c6117486c6e6b451576d11d99b6c1c9b5070a2aa58659efe2c0a0d58912cef","consequence":"LIVE as framework, KILLED as proof. Deepest existing reformulation; the missing piece (Weil positivity) is exactly RH. Gold-standard template: any future operator must reproduce this trace formula. Guardrails: D10 (reformulation, not derivation -- the hard direction is Weil positivity = RH itself); D12 (absorption 'deletes' lines from a continuum -- the continuum regularization must be audited, though Connes is explicit about it); D8 (no finite computational model of the adele class space; only finite-place truncations are computable -- which is exactly candidate B).","id":"V1","status":"killed","subject":"A. Connes adele-class trace formula (1999) -- as an RH proof","type":"V"},{"checksum":"5a56791232bec2bdc114edd9f6ed113ec61692672e2edc0b9fff793dd4a7b64e","consequence":"LIVE -- top computational target. Reimplement D_log^{(lam,N)} independently from prime Euler products; verify spectral coincidence; audit the perturbation for zero-fitting vs prime-derivation; quantify convergence error bars (D2). The only candidate that is self-adjoint by construction + prime-input-only + numerically zero-matching + finite/computable. (Per Node 11f this reimplementation was subsequently done -- the plank exists.) Guardrails: D10 -- survives forward (primes in, spectrum out) but zero-identification is numerical; D2 -- 'striking numerical accuracy' needs quantified error bars; D12 -- the rank-one perturbation direction (prime-derived vs zero-fitted) is THE question for replication; D8 -- fully computable.","id":"V2","status":"conjectural","subject":"B. Connes-Consani-Moscovici zeta spectral triples / prolate / zeta cycles (2021-2025) -- top computational target","type":"V"},{"checksum":"d1c62cf72a17601771e92c3c3af38e0d2289fd2c6a4293beb6c2c72db27a6c86","consequence":"CONJECTURAL-ONLY as theory: the missing space is the whole problem. Read, don't compute -- except a BOUNDED heuristic: concrete 3D flow with closed-orbit lengths ~ {log p : p <= z}, numerical Ruelle zeta, test for zero-like structure, labeled model-of-template from the start, never presented as evidence about zeta. Guardrails: D8 (space doesn't exist -- no direct computation); D10 (imports Weil's architecture). Note: Morishita (arXiv:2508.15971) relates this to the Connes-Consani adelic spaces; arXiv:2410.20758 proves Deninger's conjectured regularized-determinant formula in the dynamical setting (the template, not Spec Z).","id":"V3","status":"conjectural","subject":"D. Deninger foliated dynamical cohomology program (1990s-present)","type":"V"},{"checksum":"b99dccf4bf3c19c26765d20df9a229abb78a55fde2694174e107a11d7315702f","consequence":"Computation goes to B first (reimplementation from prime Euler products; audit for zero-fitting; quantify convergence), D-heuristic second (bounded, labeled model-of-template). A and the full D program are conjectural-only (read, don't compute). C, E, F, G, H are documented kills. Selberg/Mayer via the transfer operator is the control -- the one world where the full dream works (already closed as the D10d function-field template).","id":"V4","status":"heuristic","subject":"Ranked shortlist: deserves computation = B, D-heuristic; conjectural-only = A, D-full; killed = C, E, F, G, H; control = Selberg/Mayer","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","B2":"B","B3":"B","C1":"C","C2":"C","G1":"G","G2":"G","G3":"G","G4":"G","G5":"G","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","L4":"L","L5":"L","V1":"V","V2":"V","V3":"V","V4":"V"},"wire_checksum":"c696621341a94330d2c3c0d008248307934d78ed8ff91b2fcf21cb07d1cb0aaf"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1